 "rules": [
  "Pick a base variant per cell from a stable hash of (x, y), weighted by \"weights\"; rotate by (hash % 6) * 60 deg and mirror on (hash >> 3) & 1.",
  "Tiles of one type share an edge colour (\"edgeTone\"), so neighbours meet without seams; drawing them with no gap looks best for water.",
  "For every edge d of a cell, look at the neighbour across d and add the overlay whose \"on\" matches this cell and \"toward\" matches the neighbour.",
  "sand next to water gets shore_foam; the water side gets shore_lap. These are the crossing points (and dock spots).",
  "land next to water gets bank and the water side gets bank_shade: a visual \"no crossing\" edge.",
  "shallow next to deep gets deep_edge; the deep side gets shallow_edge.",
  "dock is optional and comes in two halves: dock_<d> on the beach for the edge d facing water, and dock_end_<opposite(d)> on that water neighbour.",
  "fog_<v> is a full-hex overlay for fog cells; keep the game's own fog animation on top or replace it.",
  "Draw order: base tile, edge overlays (any order), dock, then the game's tints, highlights, units."
 ],
